WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[opening theme song playing]

00:11.302 --> 00:15.181
♪ Under the cloudy sky, I saw you ♪

00:15.265 --> 00:18.268
♪ That is when our love began ♪

00:21.646 --> 00:25.567
♪ It's all complete
different shapes of us ♪

00:25.650 --> 00:29.070
♪ How did I fall in love? ♪

00:29.988 --> 00:34.367
♪ Our love story
This is like a fairy tale ♪

00:34.451 --> 00:38.079
♪ It'll be like a dream ♪

00:39.039 --> 00:44.002
♪ You and me will be true ♪

00:50.258 --> 00:51.509
[Si-woo] When I was first hired,

00:51.593 --> 00:54.804
they had me go up
and assess prevailing visibility.

00:56.556 --> 00:59.017
I go at the same time every morning,

01:00.185 --> 01:03.188
observe my unchanging targets,
the various mountains,

01:03.271 --> 01:04.731
and calculate visibility.

01:04.814 --> 01:06.274
PREVAILING VISIBILITY

01:08.610 --> 01:10.987
MOUNT INWANG
VISIBILITY: 1.6KM

01:11.071 --> 01:12.447
BAEGUNDAE PEAK

01:12.530 --> 01:14.282
MOUNT BUGAK

01:16.659 --> 01:18.745
MOUNT BUGAK
VISIBILITY: 2.9KM

01:18.828 --> 01:20.663
I always found it strange

01:20.747 --> 01:22.332
taking my measurements every day,

01:23.374 --> 01:26.252
how much we trust human eyesight

01:27.170 --> 01:29.756
that was considered good enough to be used

01:29.839 --> 01:33.176
to assess something
as important as visibility.

01:34.803 --> 01:38.014
We usually rely on machines
for their accuracy and objectivity.

01:38.097 --> 01:41.851
Human vision can be precise,
but it's more easily distorted…

01:44.771 --> 01:46.022
narrowed…

01:48.316 --> 01:49.651
or biased…

01:55.990 --> 01:57.659
by the surrounding conditions.

02:03.957 --> 02:05.959
[somber music playing]

03:02.682 --> 03:03.683
[sighs]

03:19.365 --> 03:21.367
[soft music playing]

03:39.636 --> 03:41.346
[Si-woo] Get home safe last night?

03:41.429 --> 03:42.555
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

03:56.694 --> 04:01.783
EPISODE 4
VISIBILITY

04:05.286 --> 04:07.288
[reporter 1]
We're having a cool and hazy morning,

04:07.372 --> 04:09.290
with fog in several inland areas.

04:09.374 --> 04:11.834
This is likely
due to last night's temperature drop.

04:11.918 --> 04:14.587
In addition to the fog,
visibility is quite low

04:14.671 --> 04:16.214
due to fine dust in the air.

04:16.297 --> 04:18.800
We recommend being extra careful
on the road today.

04:35.733 --> 04:37.026
[cell phone buzzes]

04:43.992 --> 04:45.201
[Si-woo] Sleep well?

04:46.577 --> 04:47.495
[sighs]

04:49.205 --> 04:50.540
If we both feel something,

04:50.623 --> 04:51.958
we date.

04:52.959 --> 04:54.335
If not, we don't.

04:54.419 --> 04:56.087
So which is it?

04:58.172 --> 05:00.675
What are… we?

05:07.223 --> 05:08.933
We work at the same place.

05:12.937 --> 05:15.273
I'm a director and you're a forecaster.

05:15.356 --> 05:16.482
That's all we are.

05:16.566 --> 05:17.567
You don't feel more?

05:17.650 --> 05:19.610
Our feelings will fade in a while.

05:19.694 --> 05:20.695
We'll be normal again.

05:20.778 --> 05:23.281
Or regret it, someday.

05:23.364 --> 05:25.033
Well, that could be nice.

05:25.116 --> 05:27.118
Remembering the one that got away.

05:27.201 --> 05:29.245
You can't ask me to date at work again.

05:29.329 --> 05:30.538
I won't.

05:31.748 --> 05:32.957
It'd be awful.

05:33.624 --> 05:34.625
I can't.

05:37.545 --> 05:40.256
How do you feel, though, about me?

05:44.469 --> 05:46.679
[wind gusting]

05:50.433 --> 05:53.853
I shouldn't have revealed it. Sorry.

06:02.403 --> 06:03.946
I'm not sorry at all.

06:04.655 --> 06:08.493
Why would I be sorry that you
could see I wanna be with you?

06:14.540 --> 06:15.583
[exhales heavily]

06:19.670 --> 06:21.172
[tires screeching]

06:21.255 --> 06:22.298
[vehicles crash]

06:22.381 --> 06:25.593
[sirens wailing]

06:29.097 --> 06:31.599
[people clamoring]

06:47.740 --> 06:50.701
[reporter 2] Due to the thick fog,
there was a 14-car pileup

06:50.785 --> 06:54.163
on the Jungang Expressway
in Hoengseong early this morning.

06:54.789 --> 06:57.667
[employee 1] We announced
to expect the fog last night.

06:57.750 --> 07:00.920
And there's been news coverage about it
in current condition since 10:00 p.m.

07:01.003 --> 07:05.174
Visibility at the time of the collision
was reported as less than 100 meters.

07:05.925 --> 07:09.095
- And how precise was our forecast?
- I'd say it was at least adequate.

07:09.178 --> 07:12.014
We reported the possibility
that visibility could drop to 50 meters

07:12.098 --> 07:14.600
if the fog in Hoengseong thickened
around 2:00 a.m.,

07:14.684 --> 07:17.937
also, we sent out texts
encouraging commuters to drive cautiously.

07:18.521 --> 07:20.189
Hmm, we did what we could.

07:21.357 --> 07:23.734
How many recent accidents
have we seen in that area?

07:24.735 --> 07:27.280
Looking at the data
from the past three years,

07:27.363 --> 07:31.200
326 cases in Daegwallyeong,
Chuncheon, 115,

07:31.284 --> 07:32.910
and 109 cases in Cheorwon.

07:33.619 --> 07:36.122
Goodness, why don't they slow down
if they know fog is so common?

07:36.205 --> 07:37.165
I don't get it.

07:38.207 --> 07:40.251
Don't you think KWA's forecast approach

07:40.334 --> 07:42.420
with fog needs to change
in response to this?

07:42.503 --> 07:45.673
Well, I'll look into it and get feedback
from the other directors.

07:47.049 --> 07:49.135
Okay. Get the meeting started, then.

07:50.136 --> 07:52.305
Let us begin the morning meeting
of May 11.

07:52.388 --> 07:53.848
Let's hear from the Satellite Center.

07:53.931 --> 07:56.058
[employee 2]
The radiative cooling has intensified

07:56.142 --> 07:58.394
- in the inland area since last night…
- [leader 1] Man.

07:58.478 --> 07:59.979
She knows what she's doing.

08:00.062 --> 08:01.481
And still single, right?

08:02.064 --> 08:03.774
Yeah, she was almost like Ms. Oh, though.

08:03.858 --> 08:05.109
Like who?

08:05.193 --> 08:06.903
Oh Myung-ju, the Assistant Director.

08:06.986 --> 08:09.197
[leader 2] Everyone thought
they'd make her director,

08:09.280 --> 08:12.033
but she married some guy here
and was always on maternity leave.

08:12.116 --> 08:14.076
They're never gonna promote her now.

08:14.160 --> 08:16.662
And how's that anything like Director Jin?

08:16.746 --> 08:18.039
[clicks tongue]
You know Mr. Han?

08:18.122 --> 08:18.998
He talks to the press.

08:19.081 --> 08:21.209
[leader 1] You mean the guy
with thick eyebrows?

08:22.043 --> 08:25.505
They were engaged, but she broke up
with him a month before the wedding.

08:25.588 --> 08:27.757
- [leader 1] She dodged the bullet, then.
- [leader 2] Hm?

08:27.840 --> 08:29.258
She's way out of his league.

08:29.342 --> 08:32.845
You're right. It's important
for women like that

08:32.929 --> 08:34.305
to find someone who's not an idiot.

08:34.388 --> 08:35.348
[both snicker]

08:35.431 --> 08:38.059
- Oh, how are your investments?
- [sighs]

08:38.893 --> 08:40.686
[leader 2] I think it's great. I…

08:49.320 --> 08:51.781
[senior reporter] It's time to come up
with something fresh.

08:51.864 --> 08:53.157
Team, circle around.

08:55.701 --> 08:56.702
Okay.

08:57.745 --> 08:59.413
What's the takeaway?

09:00.248 --> 09:01.499
Come on.

09:01.582 --> 09:04.460
Think about it, why do crashes
always happen in the same areas?

09:04.544 --> 09:05.711
[sirens wailing]

09:05.795 --> 09:06.754
Look.

09:06.837 --> 09:09.590
When it happened,
the visibility was ten meters.

09:09.674 --> 09:11.342
So, they could barely see
the filing cabinet.

09:11.425 --> 09:14.512
But what did we hear on the forecast?

09:15.721 --> 09:18.516
We don't do fog warnings.
And nowhere in Korea does, so…

09:18.599 --> 09:19.767
What are you saying?

09:19.850 --> 09:22.061
She's right. I wanna know
why we're so far behind. Hm?

09:22.144 --> 09:23.104
Other countries do.

09:23.688 --> 09:26.399
- I guess it's weird we don't.
- That's what I'm saying.

09:26.482 --> 09:28.734
So what I wanna know is, "Why?"

09:29.235 --> 09:31.654
Why do we keep
letting things like this happen?

09:31.737 --> 09:34.657
Maybe they're too worried
about covering their backs,

09:34.740 --> 09:36.867
petrified of forecasting wrong again.

09:37.660 --> 09:39.996
Find out what you can,
and get me a draft, okay?

09:40.079 --> 09:41.539
Use this accident,

09:41.622 --> 09:44.709
and pull some of the worst ones
from a couple of years ago. Okay?

09:44.792 --> 09:46.627
[sucks teeth]
Isn't this pushing a narrative?

09:46.711 --> 09:49.297
What, don't want your husband
to look bad over at KMA?

09:49.380 --> 09:50.673
Oh! Come on, it's not that.

09:50.756 --> 09:52.925
Then take your assignment and get to work.

09:53.009 --> 09:55.595
[senior reporter] A good journalist leaves
their personal life at home.

09:56.220 --> 09:57.430
So that's it.

09:57.513 --> 09:58.973
Good work. Good work. Back to it.

10:01.767 --> 10:04.186
- Okay. I'll get it.
- All right.

10:08.399 --> 10:10.860
Oh, did you go for a run before work?

10:10.943 --> 10:13.404
Oh, I thought I should come right away
after the crash.

10:13.487 --> 10:14.322
[chuckles nervously]

10:24.707 --> 10:26.167
You got home okay last night?

10:26.250 --> 10:27.835
Yeah.
[chuckles]

10:27.918 --> 10:31.505
So, hey, who was the lady
that snuck out the back?

10:31.589 --> 10:34.175
Who? He was with a woman?

10:35.176 --> 10:37.720
Uh, I really don't know
what you're even talking about.

10:37.803 --> 10:39.639
You do. I know what I saw.

10:39.722 --> 10:41.682
There was this woman at your table,

10:41.766 --> 10:43.684
and she snuck out
the very second we arrived.

10:43.768 --> 10:44.810
[Myung-ju] What?

10:45.436 --> 10:47.021
You have a girlfriend?

10:52.568 --> 10:54.111
No. Not right now.

10:54.195 --> 10:56.739
You're lying to us. Your poker face sucks.

10:56.822 --> 10:59.825
You can't hide someone
you really care about. You'll slip up.

11:05.706 --> 11:07.416
Well, it's not official yet.

11:07.500 --> 11:09.669
Aw, look at you.
You're dating so soon again.

11:09.752 --> 11:12.505
It's good, though.
How'd you meet? A blind date?

11:12.588 --> 11:13.714
At a club in town?

11:14.215 --> 11:17.259
- No, it was through work, actually.
- [gasps]

11:17.343 --> 11:19.345
Does she work at KMA?

11:19.428 --> 11:21.222
Do we… Just tell us her name.

11:21.305 --> 11:22.473
[Myung-ju] Did you meet at HQ?

11:22.556 --> 11:23.599
She works here?

11:24.266 --> 11:25.351
Forecaster Lee!

11:29.021 --> 11:32.066
I need a distribution chart
on the fog in Hoengseong

11:32.149 --> 11:33.818
an hour before and after the collision,

11:33.901 --> 11:35.778
and please make it
in ten-minute intervals.

11:38.072 --> 11:39.240
Maybe I should repeat myself?

11:39.323 --> 11:40.658
Oh, no, I got it all.

11:40.741 --> 11:44.161
One hour before and after the collision
in ten-minute intervals.

11:44.787 --> 11:46.414
You'll have it soon?

11:46.497 --> 11:48.457
Yeah, of course. Right away.

11:50.084 --> 11:51.502
What?

11:51.585 --> 11:53.170
She's messing with him, right?

11:53.254 --> 11:55.714
She must be. Maybe he did something?

11:55.798 --> 11:58.008
- [keyboard clacking]
- [cell phone buzzing]

11:58.092 --> 11:59.718
DREAM REALTY

12:02.054 --> 12:04.557
- Yes?
- [realtor] Slight setback.

12:04.640 --> 12:06.934
The buyers reached out,
they went to the bank,

12:07.017 --> 12:09.603
they're backing out of the deal.

12:09.687 --> 12:10.604
Why?

12:10.688 --> 12:12.815
They had issues finalizing the bank loan.

12:13.399 --> 12:15.401
- I see.
- So, what now?

12:15.484 --> 12:18.362
Lower the price?
Going below market will sell it.

12:20.281 --> 12:21.699
So what do you think?

12:22.324 --> 12:24.452
Do it if you want to sell it quickly.

12:24.535 --> 12:29.540
[keyboard clacking]

12:30.332 --> 12:33.335
Give me some time to think about it,
and then I'll call you.

12:51.145 --> 12:53.147
[somber music playing]

12:54.690 --> 12:55.524
[sighs]

13:06.994 --> 13:09.413
[leader 2] You know Mr. Han?
He talks to the press.

13:09.497 --> 13:13.000
They were engaged, but she broke up
with him a month before the wedding.

13:13.083 --> 13:15.211
- [leader 1] She dodged the bullet, then.
- [leader 2] Hm?

13:15.294 --> 13:16.795
She's way out of his league.

13:16.879 --> 13:19.089
You're right. It's important
for women like that

13:19.173 --> 13:21.050
to find someone who's not an idiot.

13:21.133 --> 13:22.343
[both snicker]

13:29.308 --> 13:31.101
[Ju-won] What's happened to your writing?

13:31.894 --> 13:33.062
There's a problem?

13:33.145 --> 13:35.648
I know there won't be any eyes
on it outside of KMA,

13:35.731 --> 13:38.359
but still, this is sloppy.

13:38.442 --> 13:40.027
Your last column was, too.

13:40.110 --> 13:42.696
We don't need anyone saying,
"Careful not to catch a cold."

13:42.780 --> 13:45.741
Our mothers say it enough.
I want us to have more substance. Okay?

13:46.408 --> 13:47.910
You didn't mention any issues before.

13:48.494 --> 13:50.412
I thought you were just distracted.

13:50.496 --> 13:53.582
The wedding was right around the corner,
I thought it was nerves.

13:53.666 --> 13:55.292
[Ju-won inhales sharply]

13:55.376 --> 13:58.045
You're not back on track yet,
so I'm getting worried.

13:58.128 --> 14:00.923
I don't know.
Fix it on the next one. Okay?

14:01.006 --> 14:02.633
You need to get it together.

14:03.384 --> 14:04.593
I didn't think it was sloppy.

14:07.054 --> 14:08.514
- Sorry, sir.
- Listen.

14:08.597 --> 14:10.266
In front of the cameras, you're great.

14:10.349 --> 14:12.893
Just give a quarter of that
to writing, okay?

14:12.977 --> 14:14.228
I'll fix it, sir.

14:15.145 --> 14:16.647
I need you alert, yeah?

14:17.231 --> 14:18.232
Yes, sir.

14:18.315 --> 14:19.650
- [shouts] Yeah?
- Yes!

14:20.484 --> 14:21.819
[in normal voice]
Fix it.

14:21.902 --> 14:23.904
[retreating footsteps]

14:33.038 --> 14:34.039
[groans]

14:42.214 --> 14:43.465
Did he yell at you?

14:44.008 --> 14:45.676
No, he didn't.

14:45.759 --> 14:47.428
Well, then what did he say to you?

14:47.511 --> 14:49.221
Uh, it was nothing.

14:50.848 --> 14:53.100
So, what can I do for you?

14:53.726 --> 14:57.313
Oh… The huge pileup on the expressway
in Hoengseong,

14:57.396 --> 14:59.356
it was 'cause of the fog, right?

14:59.440 --> 15:01.650
What do you mean?
The forecast was adequate.

15:01.734 --> 15:02.902
I heard that.

15:02.985 --> 15:05.613
I'd like to interview someone
about the accident.

15:05.696 --> 15:08.407
Can you get someone from the Chief Team
who will answer my questions?

15:10.200 --> 15:12.077
It's not a great time. Later, though.

15:12.161 --> 15:14.496
My deadline for the article is insane.

15:14.580 --> 15:16.582
'Cause it's due by the end of the day.

15:16.665 --> 15:18.834
Do you know how busy Chief Team is?

15:18.918 --> 15:21.879
They have more important things to do
than meet your deadlines.

15:21.962 --> 15:23.672
Well, you don't have to use that tone.

15:23.756 --> 15:25.424
You're a spokesperson.

15:25.507 --> 15:29.428
Is it so wrong to ask for a spokesperson
to coordinate an interview?

15:29.511 --> 15:31.722
- Look.
- I'm a reporter.

15:31.805 --> 15:34.558
I know. I'll try to fit it in, okay?

15:34.642 --> 15:36.185
I need to handle something first.

15:36.268 --> 15:38.312
Whatever. It's fine.

15:43.108 --> 15:44.526
[groans]

15:44.610 --> 15:45.694
Jeez.

15:46.445 --> 15:49.156
There's already way too much to do.

15:49.239 --> 15:51.700
You're making it even harder.

15:51.784 --> 15:53.077
[sighs]

15:53.702 --> 15:55.079
Why?

16:06.507 --> 16:07.549
[sighs]

16:19.770 --> 16:21.689
Here's the data you wanted, ma'am.

16:21.772 --> 16:24.149
I don't really understand
what you want it for, but it's completed.

16:24.233 --> 16:28.570
I'd appreciate if you'd avoid small talk
during working hours, Forecaster Lee.

16:33.534 --> 16:35.119
Thanks for this. You may go.

16:35.202 --> 16:37.413
[playful music playing]

16:38.372 --> 16:39.999
Yes? Can I help you?

16:40.082 --> 16:42.251
Uh, no. I'm all good.

16:49.675 --> 16:52.011
He definitely did something.

16:52.094 --> 16:53.262
[Soo-jin] Definitely.

17:06.775 --> 17:07.818
Here you go.

17:10.195 --> 17:11.238
[clears throat]

17:11.739 --> 17:12.573
What did you do?

17:13.824 --> 17:16.744
- What?
- You did something to make her upset.

17:17.494 --> 17:19.621
Well, I made a little small talk at work.

17:20.539 --> 17:23.584
You and I both know she wouldn't
normally care about something like that.

17:24.251 --> 17:25.335
So?

17:27.129 --> 17:29.673
What are… we?

17:30.549 --> 17:31.925
We work at the same place.

17:32.009 --> 17:33.510
That's all we are.

17:34.887 --> 17:36.722
Well, she's putting up a wall.

17:37.347 --> 17:39.808
Why would she feel
like she has to do that, though?

17:39.892 --> 17:42.519
"Just 'cause I'm young
doesn't mean I'm less of a director.

17:42.603 --> 17:45.230
Cut the attitude right now
and fall in line, rookie."

17:46.023 --> 17:47.107
Could that be a clue?

17:47.191 --> 17:48.776
You were rude to her?

17:48.859 --> 17:50.194
Oh!

17:52.696 --> 17:55.365
I told you HQ is too strict for you.

17:55.449 --> 17:57.826
Huh? It's not like the Metro Office.

17:57.910 --> 17:59.536
Oh, man.

18:01.080 --> 18:02.998
It's worse
that it's Director Jin Ha-kyung.

18:03.082 --> 18:06.001
I never met
such a detail-oriented perfectionist.

18:06.627 --> 18:10.214
You know, she's more conservative
than I expected her to be.

18:10.297 --> 18:12.424
She's not like you,
going with the flow, here and there.

18:12.508 --> 18:13.967
It'll probably get worse.

18:14.510 --> 18:15.886
And so it is.
[chuckles]

18:18.138 --> 18:19.723
Anyway, find a place?

18:19.807 --> 18:20.766
Not yet.

18:21.266 --> 18:24.394
'Cause everything is out of my budget,
or they're way too small and run-down.

18:25.562 --> 18:27.564
Do you have any leads?

18:27.648 --> 18:28.649
Oh, no, I don't.

18:28.732 --> 18:30.901
I just thought that you needed a reminder.

18:30.984 --> 18:34.071
Oh, and uh, try to be good
and listen to Director Jin.

18:34.154 --> 18:36.448
Don't put too much into dating right now.

18:36.532 --> 18:37.699
You don't have time.

18:38.450 --> 18:39.409
[scoffs]

18:47.334 --> 18:49.920
[Ha-kyung] The surface temperature
will drop again tomorrow morning

18:50.003 --> 18:52.297
from radiative cooling, correct?

18:52.381 --> 18:56.051
Oh, yeah. There'll be a big difference
between day and night temperatures.

18:56.760 --> 19:00.848
Since it's gonna be similar,
we can use yesterday's follow-up report--

19:00.931 --> 19:03.100
Maybe we should extend the range?

19:03.183 --> 19:04.935
[Si-woo] That would be
too wide to be useful.

19:05.769 --> 19:07.396
What if we break down each area?

19:07.479 --> 19:13.068
And we can emphasize the valleys,
streams, and any other unique areas.

19:15.279 --> 19:18.866
So we know that the fog
is the worst between 3:00 and 7:00 a.m.

19:18.949 --> 19:22.619
And in that window, most people
are on the expressway, not roads.

19:25.581 --> 19:26.999
[Ha-kyung] You're getting too close.

19:27.082 --> 19:30.460
It doesn't solve how different conditions
are within the region.

19:30.544 --> 19:33.046
Look at route over three,
it gets a lot of sun.

19:33.130 --> 19:35.799
We can expect that fog
to clear up by sunrise.

19:37.092 --> 19:38.969
[Si-woo] Too close. And it bothers you?

19:42.055 --> 19:46.143
According to the observational data
you recorded yesterday,

19:46.226 --> 19:47.394
you saw high humidity?

19:47.978 --> 19:49.938
I know that region really well.

19:50.022 --> 19:53.275
Everyone expects the fog
to be very intense this time of year.

19:53.358 --> 19:54.484
[scoffs]

19:54.568 --> 19:56.486
You sure are an expert in everything.

19:57.070 --> 19:59.072
You knew all about the climate
in the West Sea

19:59.156 --> 20:00.532
from being onboard the weather ship,

20:00.616 --> 20:03.493
and you're well-versed in the fog patterns
in Gangwon Province, too?

20:03.577 --> 20:05.954
I was on that weather ship
and I happened to work in Gangwon.

20:06.038 --> 20:09.416
And I'm confident that I know the terrain
of those areas like the back of my hand.

20:09.499 --> 20:11.376
And I'm accounting for the climate change.

20:11.460 --> 20:14.213
I consider all my life experiences
to be like live data.

20:14.296 --> 20:16.506
You've only seen them through computers,
I am the expert.

20:17.257 --> 20:19.843
- Then what do you recommend?
- It's up to you.

20:19.927 --> 20:21.595
You could break it down by area, though.

20:27.893 --> 20:28.936
I say…

20:29.645 --> 20:31.146
We give a regional warning.

20:31.230 --> 20:34.608
No, we have to separate it into areas,
and give warnings to each one.

20:34.691 --> 20:36.401
At least for every bridge and tunnel.

20:36.485 --> 20:39.029
- It's not up to you.
- When you all doubted the hail

20:39.112 --> 20:40.364
and that it will rain,

20:41.281 --> 20:42.407
I knew it was coming.

20:47.621 --> 20:51.333
Oh, given the time of year
and how often there are accidents

20:51.416 --> 20:55.128
all along the expressway,
a regional warning would be enough.

20:55.212 --> 20:56.213
Did you hear that?

20:56.296 --> 21:01.051
I see how a breakdown by area
could be useful if we give details.

21:01.134 --> 21:04.304
- He gets it.
- Regardless, because we know

21:04.388 --> 21:08.308
that Gangwon is almost guaranteed
to be foggy tomorrow morning,

21:08.392 --> 21:11.228
we can start working
on a preliminary report, right?

21:11.311 --> 21:12.521
That way, we're not waiting on you.

21:12.604 --> 21:15.107
- I think we need… Well…
- Without a full plan?

21:15.691 --> 21:18.068
Of course, we can touch base
throughout the day.

21:18.735 --> 21:21.822
And if we can agree on a plan,
then it turns to the night team's concern.

21:22.322 --> 21:24.032
We're late. We have to get a report done.

21:26.118 --> 21:26.952
Right?

21:29.997 --> 21:30.956
Right?

21:31.623 --> 21:32.749
[Si-woo] I'm calling from HQ.

21:32.833 --> 21:34.793
Uh, we sent over some information
about the fog.

21:34.876 --> 21:36.086
Did it go through?

21:36.670 --> 21:37.879
Oh, good.

21:37.963 --> 21:41.633
Please send out a fog warning
for tomorrow morning to the entire region.

21:41.717 --> 21:43.302
As for breakdowns by area?

21:48.598 --> 21:51.476
I'll write them out myself,
and I'll call back with some updates.

21:51.560 --> 21:52.602
Thanks.

21:55.439 --> 21:56.606
[sighs]

22:04.239 --> 22:07.034
CUSTOMER SURPRISE SERVICE INDEX
CATEGORY: MATCHMAKING SERVICE

22:07.117 --> 22:09.953
SEOUL AWARD CERTIFICATE
NUBO, MATCHMAKING SERVICE

22:11.455 --> 22:14.416
You said your daughter
is, um, a Class Five civil servant?

22:14.499 --> 22:16.209
Ah, yes.
[chuckles]

22:16.293 --> 22:19.004
And she didn't just wait to level up.

22:19.087 --> 22:21.006
[Mrs. Bae] They chose her
from a pool of recruits,

22:21.089 --> 22:23.342
since her test scores
were second best of anyone there.

22:23.425 --> 22:24.509
Wow.

22:24.593 --> 22:27.596
Ma, let's go home. We can leave.

22:27.679 --> 22:28.764
Don't say anything.

22:28.847 --> 22:30.766
Ha-kyung's never gonna speak to you again.

22:30.849 --> 22:32.768
If you're so scared, then you should go.

22:32.851 --> 22:33.935
[woman] All right.

22:34.019 --> 22:35.437
Oh, did she do well?

22:35.520 --> 22:38.315
One minute.
Based on her algorithm, she is…

22:38.398 --> 22:41.693
Come on, it's Ha-kyung.
I'm sure she's ranked very high.

22:41.777 --> 22:44.112
She's like galbi beef, the best.

22:44.196 --> 22:46.865
Ma, don't say she's like beef.
That's so weird.

22:46.948 --> 22:48.492
Ha-kyung's not a piece of meat.

22:49.076 --> 22:51.036
Will you stop?
[clicks tongue]

22:51.912 --> 22:53.121
[clears throat]

22:53.205 --> 22:54.998
- She places at Level Eight.
- What?

22:55.749 --> 22:57.000
How is she Level Eight?

22:57.084 --> 23:00.504
No, please don't worry.
Level Eight is quite respectable.

23:00.587 --> 23:01.797
[woman chuckles]

23:01.880 --> 23:04.216
[coughing]

23:04.299 --> 23:07.928
You said my Ha-kyung is only Level Eight?
I don't understand.

23:08.011 --> 23:10.639
She scored in the top percentile
of every test she's taken

23:10.722 --> 23:11.765
since she was a kid.

23:11.848 --> 23:13.558
Well, this is no standard test.

23:13.642 --> 23:16.394
We say marriage
is one family joining the other.

23:16.478 --> 23:19.231
And because of that,
we look beyond a person's job.

23:19.314 --> 23:21.483
Personal information plays a big role.

23:21.566 --> 23:24.444
But so do the parents and siblings,

23:24.528 --> 23:27.614
everything is taken into account
to determine the ranking.

23:27.697 --> 23:28.907
So you…

23:29.699 --> 23:32.452
lowered her score,
because I'm a single mother?

23:32.536 --> 23:35.080
No, that's not what I said. It's not that.

23:35.580 --> 23:37.666
Obviously, you did
a great job raising her.

23:37.749 --> 23:39.209
The bigger issue is your income.

23:39.292 --> 23:41.920
It's almost impossible
to raise two kids on your own,

23:42.003 --> 23:44.214
then you expect me to get rich
while doing it?

23:44.798 --> 23:46.049
[Mrs. Bae] Ridiculous.

23:46.133 --> 23:48.176
See, Ma? I told you it's a waste of time.

23:48.969 --> 23:50.137
I should clarify,

23:50.220 --> 23:52.848
parents need more than 20 billion won
to make the top level.

23:55.058 --> 23:58.812
Honestly, there are a lot of doctors,
even lawyers that only rank Level Seven.

23:58.895 --> 24:03.358
Even doctors and lawyers
can rank as low as Level Seven?

24:03.441 --> 24:05.610
That's what I'm trying to tell you, ma'am.

24:05.694 --> 24:06.903
Level Eight is full of

24:06.987 --> 24:09.823
all sorts of public servants,
even public officials.

24:09.906 --> 24:11.741
There's no reason to be worried at all.

24:11.825 --> 24:13.410
I guarantee we'll find someone

24:13.493 --> 24:16.413
that is at least an equal
for your daughter.

24:16.496 --> 24:17.581
Come on.

24:18.582 --> 24:20.083
[gasps]

24:21.084 --> 24:22.377
Hmm…

24:27.132 --> 24:28.508
[exhales deeply]

24:31.261 --> 24:32.470
Now is a fun part.

24:32.554 --> 24:35.265
We get to make the plan
of how we'll get her to her wedding day.

24:35.348 --> 24:36.433
Are you ready?

24:40.103 --> 24:42.772
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

24:44.566 --> 24:46.318
You've been busy all day.

24:46.401 --> 24:49.988
Yeah, I have this high-priority article,
and I've got to get an interview.

24:53.366 --> 24:55.535
What? What did you wanna say?

24:55.619 --> 24:59.080
It's the forecaster from before,
Lee Si-woo, right?

25:00.457 --> 25:02.000
Yeah, I really don't know the guy.

25:02.083 --> 25:04.794
Well, I heard a rumor
he broke up with his girlfriend.

25:06.254 --> 25:07.339
So?

25:08.381 --> 25:10.008
Introduce us.

25:10.091 --> 25:11.092
[chuckles]

25:12.219 --> 25:14.387
You have so many other options,
it seems risky.

25:14.471 --> 25:17.265
I don't know why you'd wanna date
a co-worker, anyway.

25:17.349 --> 25:18.767
People will be all in your business.

25:18.850 --> 25:20.518
It wouldn't be that bad.

25:21.186 --> 25:24.773
Work's so boring. We sit and write
and don't talk to anyone.

25:25.315 --> 25:27.943
I mean, it worked for you. Please?

25:28.026 --> 25:28.902
We'll see.

25:28.985 --> 25:31.071
We're not really that close.
I don't know him.

25:31.154 --> 25:32.280
You're better off on your own.

25:34.783 --> 25:36.451
Chae Yu-jin. Hey.

25:36.534 --> 25:38.787
Ugh, come on.

25:48.213 --> 25:50.215
[quirky music playing]

25:52.384 --> 25:55.345
I can't believe how popular Mr. Lee is
with the girls, you know?

25:56.179 --> 25:57.180
It's silly.

25:57.264 --> 26:00.392
It really makes me wonder.
Who could he be dating from the office?

26:01.059 --> 26:03.228
I think it's best to just ignore it all.

26:06.064 --> 26:08.358
I wish I could. I just need to know
since she's here.

26:09.192 --> 26:10.235
Oh, she's here?

26:10.318 --> 26:12.237
Well, he said they met at work.

26:12.320 --> 26:16.032
It could be someone from the Metro Office,
then she might not be here at all.

26:16.116 --> 26:17.909
I saw her, so she must be here.

26:17.993 --> 26:21.162
We showed up, and she started crawling
through the back door.

26:21.246 --> 26:23.623
If she's not here,
why would she try and hide?

26:23.707 --> 26:25.959
I heard him say they're not official.

26:26.042 --> 26:28.336
At least I thought I did, earlier.

26:28.420 --> 26:30.297
And so I take it that you heard it all.

26:30.380 --> 26:33.967
Accidentally, if you're in the same room,
you hear things.

26:34.551 --> 26:36.803
I just hope you're not
being too hard on him.

26:36.886 --> 26:38.555
He's just new. Don't hate him.

26:39.180 --> 26:40.557
I don't hate anyone.

26:42.559 --> 26:45.270
All right, I'll keep you updated.
I'm gonna find her.

26:45.353 --> 26:46.521
[chuckles]

26:46.604 --> 26:48.315
It's just a matter of time now.

26:55.071 --> 26:56.281
Ugh.

26:56.364 --> 26:58.575
[Ha-kyung] Office romance
will be the death of me.

26:59.701 --> 27:00.994
THE ATMOSPHERE

27:01.077 --> 27:02.829
[Seok-ho] Okay, should we get out of here?

27:04.664 --> 27:06.249
- See you tomorrow.
- Goodbye.

27:06.333 --> 27:07.584
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

27:09.127 --> 27:10.670
Ah… Uh-oh.

27:11.171 --> 27:13.965
The night team should take over all that.

27:14.049 --> 27:17.677
Why waste all your time writing out
the fog breakdown yourself?

27:17.761 --> 27:20.889
I made a promise to the Gangwon Office
that I'd send it by midnight.

27:20.972 --> 27:23.683
Ugh, I said to watch your attitude,
not be teacher's pet.

27:23.767 --> 27:26.269
Well, actually, I thought
this might help her like me more.

27:26.353 --> 27:27.437
Jeez.

27:27.520 --> 27:29.522
- Don't pull an all-nighter, okay?
- Okay.

27:29.606 --> 27:30.857
- See you.
- Good luck.

27:43.828 --> 27:45.205
Got it under control?

27:46.206 --> 27:47.665
Yup. I'm good. Thanks.

27:48.583 --> 27:50.168
Okay. Goodbye, then.

27:50.251 --> 27:51.252
Bye.

27:53.463 --> 27:54.881
Turn around.

27:54.964 --> 27:57.008
[Si-woo] Turn around.

27:57.801 --> 27:59.010
Turn around.

28:00.845 --> 28:02.180
She didn't do it.

28:04.265 --> 28:05.767
[groans]

28:09.771 --> 28:11.773
[quirky music playing]

28:13.316 --> 28:14.275
[elevator dings]

28:14.359 --> 28:15.944
[female voice] Doors opening.

28:28.248 --> 28:29.624
Doors closing.

28:31.543 --> 28:33.545
[somber music playing]

28:42.554 --> 28:43.972
[elevator chimes]

28:49.811 --> 28:50.979
Excuse me.

28:52.814 --> 28:54.357
Would you do an interview?

28:55.442 --> 28:56.651
An interview for what?

28:58.278 --> 28:59.904
It's for an article I'm writing.

28:59.988 --> 29:01.865
I need an opinion from a director.

29:02.532 --> 29:04.784
I understand if it's too uncomfortable.

29:14.753 --> 29:18.673
THEMED STORY FOR JUNE

29:20.300 --> 29:21.885
[Ha-kyung] You have writer's block?

29:24.012 --> 29:25.096
Mm-hm.

29:29.559 --> 29:31.311
What's this? In May?

29:31.394 --> 29:33.062
- That's the front?
- Mm.

29:33.146 --> 29:34.272
[Ha-kyung] Hm…

29:36.858 --> 29:38.151
May…

29:39.360 --> 29:42.822
In May, the weather is nice,
so people go outside more.

29:42.906 --> 29:43.782
Mm-hm.

29:44.866 --> 29:48.286
You could do some tips
on how to plan using our forecast.

29:48.369 --> 29:49.704
- You think?
- Mm-hm.

29:50.622 --> 29:52.499
And then for the title…

29:52.582 --> 29:57.545
You could do,
"Reading Forecast Like Professionals."

29:57.629 --> 29:58.880
- It's good.
- It's too wordy.

29:58.963 --> 30:00.048
- I think it's great.
- Really?

30:00.131 --> 30:00.965
- Yeah.
- Okay.

30:01.049 --> 30:03.134
- "Reading… Forecast…"
- "Forecast."

30:03.218 --> 30:06.054
- "Like the Professional…"
- "Like Professionals."

30:06.137 --> 30:08.598
Then you just say what you do,
how they can get

30:08.681 --> 30:10.517
the most out of the forecast.

30:10.600 --> 30:12.602
[somber music playing]

30:16.397 --> 30:17.440
[sighs]

30:35.875 --> 30:38.336
So, there have been lots
of accidents from the fog lately.

30:38.962 --> 30:41.047
There isn't anything very special
about the recent fog.

30:41.130 --> 30:42.924
The DTR is predictably high

30:43.007 --> 30:46.010
in February, April, and May,
August, and October,

30:46.094 --> 30:49.514
so expect a certain amount of fog
in those months.

30:49.597 --> 30:52.308
Accidents predictably go up,
then, as well.

30:52.392 --> 30:54.227
Regionally, though, there have been a lot

30:54.310 --> 30:57.564
of fog-related accidents
in Gangwon, specifically.

30:57.647 --> 31:01.067
If you check the Seohae Bridge,
it likely has many accidents.

31:02.318 --> 31:06.322
So then, why is our country behind
on implementing fog advisories?

31:07.991 --> 31:08.950
Um…

31:09.033 --> 31:10.535
It would be difficult to do them here,

31:10.618 --> 31:12.745
because of the geography
around the country.

31:12.829 --> 31:14.873
Accurate fog advisories would take

31:14.956 --> 31:18.251
a different type of equipment
for monitoring moisture particles.

31:18.334 --> 31:20.003
We need them set up every two kilometers.

31:20.086 --> 31:23.631
And it'd be impossible to do
on the budget allotted for KMA.

31:23.715 --> 31:26.759
So it's an issue of not
having enough money or equipment?

31:26.843 --> 31:28.261
And there's nothing we can do?

31:31.639 --> 31:33.766
Is there an angle you're trying to push?

31:34.392 --> 31:36.144
The only angle I'm looking for
is the truth.

31:38.605 --> 31:42.942
It's true that the recent collision
on the expressway happened

31:43.026 --> 31:45.570
because the visibility
was quite low from the fog.

31:46.362 --> 31:49.490
But we did forecast the fog,
we just couldn't say exact visibility.

31:50.074 --> 31:52.660
- Is that true enough for you?
- I think that's up to the public.

31:52.744 --> 31:54.037
They have the final say here.

32:02.879 --> 32:03.755
[sighs]

32:04.339 --> 32:05.882
Things okay at your house?

32:05.965 --> 32:07.425
Man, I…

32:08.468 --> 32:10.637
- Everything's all right.
- Really?

32:12.388 --> 32:15.016
It could be awkward, and then it won't be.

32:15.975 --> 32:17.185
Hey.

32:17.268 --> 32:18.853
Was it like that for you?

32:20.813 --> 32:22.398
You know where I stand.

32:22.482 --> 32:25.568
I always hated being away from my family
and I'd fight it when I could.

32:25.652 --> 32:28.404
And if I couldn't, I bring them
to wherever I was dispatched.

32:28.488 --> 32:31.074
- Hm.
- It was only two years

32:31.157 --> 32:34.410
that we were fully separated,
when my kid was getting ready for college.

32:34.494 --> 32:35.745
Ah.

32:35.828 --> 32:37.956
When my term was finally over,

32:38.665 --> 32:41.376
it took a long time
before things were normal again.

32:41.459 --> 32:43.878
So? So, I've gotta wait it out.

32:44.462 --> 32:46.714
I… That's not what I said at all.

32:46.798 --> 32:49.050
You can't just wait.
You have to take initiative.

32:49.133 --> 32:50.718
You have to push. Okay?

32:50.802 --> 32:53.680
If you keep withdrawing
because it's hard and awkward,

32:53.763 --> 32:56.265
you're just gonna stay an outsider
in your own family.

32:56.349 --> 32:57.350
Get it?

32:58.935 --> 33:00.937
At least, that's how it felt for us.

33:01.020 --> 33:02.522
It's food for thought.

33:02.605 --> 33:03.982
[sighs]
Right.

33:05.942 --> 33:10.071
How long do you think
until I feel like it's home again?

33:10.154 --> 33:11.364
Does that come back?

33:11.447 --> 33:13.199
Months, tops? A year?

33:13.282 --> 33:15.493
It depends on if you push.

33:16.369 --> 33:17.537
Makes sense.

33:36.222 --> 33:37.432
Hey.

33:42.979 --> 33:44.147
[chuckles]

33:45.023 --> 33:47.150
Watching something funny?
[chuckles]

33:49.569 --> 33:51.404
- Show me.
- [grunts]

33:52.071 --> 33:54.407
You can't just look at my phone.

33:55.324 --> 33:56.743
I didn't see anything.

33:59.746 --> 34:01.956
We're family. So what if I did?

34:03.958 --> 34:05.168
[sighs]

34:08.212 --> 34:09.297
[door slams]

34:12.508 --> 34:14.093
[sighs]

34:16.137 --> 34:20.975
[pot clinking]

34:26.522 --> 34:29.192
Do you need my help with anything?

34:29.275 --> 34:30.359
[Hyang-rae] I'm set.

34:30.985 --> 34:32.487
[Dong-han] Here. I'll get it. Let me…

34:32.570 --> 34:33.696
- [Hyang-rae] Wait!
- [clatters]

34:33.780 --> 34:35.364
- [Dong-han] Ooh!
- [Hyang-rae] Ahh!

34:35.448 --> 34:36.908
[Hyang-rae sighs]

34:36.991 --> 34:38.534
- Oh, shoot.
- Oh, no.

34:38.618 --> 34:40.661
You've gotta be kidding me, Dong-han.

34:40.745 --> 34:42.955
Why couldn't you just listen?

34:43.039 --> 34:45.583
Instead of rushing in and making a mess?

34:45.666 --> 34:48.086
I thought I should help my wife.

34:48.169 --> 34:50.671
You can't help if you don't know
what you're doing.

34:50.755 --> 34:52.632
You have no idea how we do things.

34:55.134 --> 34:58.679
Don't you think that you…
you're being really harsh about things?

34:59.847 --> 35:02.850
Whatever. I'm sorry we had
to live apart for 14 years.

35:03.851 --> 35:05.561
I had no choice. I had to go.

35:06.687 --> 35:09.607
What, you think I wanted
to leave you, huh?

35:09.690 --> 35:13.486
You know there was no way.
It was too expensive to move everyone.

35:14.237 --> 35:16.697
I have always been faithful to you,
you know?

35:17.323 --> 35:19.283
My first priority is providing for you.

35:19.367 --> 35:23.913
So it'd mean a lot if you could just say,
"We missed you. Thanks for your work."

35:23.996 --> 35:26.457
It's been 14 years,
and you can't say that once?

35:27.041 --> 35:29.335
I see people more excited
about a dog coming home.

35:29.418 --> 35:31.838
Are you… Are you gonna punish me forever?

35:33.214 --> 35:34.382
[sighs]

35:35.341 --> 35:37.093
- Is that all?
- No.

35:38.094 --> 35:40.096
You think that sending money every month

35:40.179 --> 35:43.516
and not cheating even once
was all we needed from you?

35:44.100 --> 35:47.061
What else? More?
What more could you need from me?

35:48.020 --> 35:50.356
Do you remember when Bo-mi was born?

35:52.400 --> 35:53.693
Yeah, she was…

35:53.776 --> 35:55.153
I was on…

35:55.236 --> 35:57.488
You were on a weather ship
out in the South Sea.

35:58.072 --> 35:59.907
You didn't even meet her
for the first time

35:59.991 --> 36:01.450
until she was three months old.

36:01.534 --> 36:04.287
Right. There was nothing I could do.

36:04.370 --> 36:06.706
What happened on her first day of school?

36:07.874 --> 36:09.750
First day of school, I was…

36:09.834 --> 36:13.254
On Baengnyeong Island,
you sent her one text.

36:14.005 --> 36:16.591
I know. We already went over that one.

36:16.674 --> 36:18.593
The way things were back then,

36:18.676 --> 36:20.887
there wasn't any time for me to get away.

36:20.970 --> 36:22.847
Right. Nothing you could do, again.

36:24.932 --> 36:26.017
Oh, and you should know.

36:27.310 --> 36:31.606
Everyone in this neighborhood thought
I was raising her on my own.

36:31.689 --> 36:32.815
They what?

36:33.566 --> 36:35.234
Who said? Tell me who said that.

36:35.318 --> 36:36.402
[scoffs]

36:37.236 --> 36:38.905
The whole neighborhood.

36:40.114 --> 36:41.616
When Bo-mi got sick,

36:41.699 --> 36:44.994
I strapped her to my back
and carried her to the hospital.

36:45.828 --> 36:48.372
If I brought her
to the grocery store with me,

36:48.456 --> 36:49.457
we'd get free food,

36:49.540 --> 36:52.376
'cause even the bag boy thought
I was a single mom.

36:54.337 --> 36:56.505
I had to figure out how to tell the truth.

36:57.632 --> 36:59.258
All you care about is weather.

36:59.342 --> 37:02.803
Any kind of weather,
you'll go sun, you'll go storm, you'll go.

37:02.887 --> 37:06.432
You'll wander around the whole world,
and maybe stop at home for a day.

37:06.515 --> 37:09.101
Then the next morning, you'd tell me
you would have to leave again

37:09.185 --> 37:10.394
for some stupid reason, right?

37:10.478 --> 37:12.271
You were never there. Ever.

37:15.149 --> 37:17.026
So we've tried to move on.

37:17.985 --> 37:20.404
We've made it 14 years without you.

37:21.697 --> 37:23.532
You understand me now?

37:46.138 --> 37:47.139
[door shuts]

38:15.918 --> 38:19.130
THEMED STORY FOR JUNE

38:33.644 --> 38:35.730
[groaning]

38:41.694 --> 38:42.695
MESSAGE FROM SPACE

38:42.778 --> 38:44.280
AN INTRODUCTION
TO DYNAMIC METEOROLOGY

38:44.363 --> 38:47.158
THE ENCYCLOPEDIA
OF WEATHER AND CLIMATE CHANGE

38:58.669 --> 39:00.129
THOSE WHO FIGHT WEATHER

39:00.212 --> 39:03.341
"Those Who Fight Weather. By Chae Yu-jin."

39:10.181 --> 39:11.807
Ah, cute.

39:11.891 --> 39:13.517
[chuckles]

39:25.112 --> 39:26.947
Hey, is everything okay?

39:27.656 --> 39:30.368
Wasn't he that psycho
that tried to wreck the wedding?

39:30.451 --> 39:33.579
Who? That guy?
No, there's absolutely no way.

39:34.580 --> 39:35.706
Are you sure?

39:35.790 --> 39:38.042
[scoffs]
Wouldn't that be wild?

39:45.341 --> 39:46.258
[sighs]

39:54.183 --> 39:55.351
[exhales deeply]

39:57.686 --> 40:00.147
WHY DOESN'T KOREA…

40:17.957 --> 40:19.875
[gasps]
Oh, my god.

40:22.044 --> 40:23.170
[scoffs]

40:23.254 --> 40:25.881
- Is she really gonna kill me?
- No.

40:28.384 --> 40:30.678
Maybe I should have asked her
before signing her up.

40:30.761 --> 40:32.138
[scoffs]
Wow.

40:33.097 --> 40:36.517
Did you hear any of what I was saying
before we met with that lady?

40:36.600 --> 40:37.768
See, I told you.

40:37.852 --> 40:39.478
Of course, we should have asked her first.

40:40.438 --> 40:41.897
I did it, because it's best for her.

40:41.981 --> 40:43.566
More like it's best for you.

40:43.649 --> 40:45.693
You're embarrassed to tell people
that they called off the wedding

40:45.776 --> 40:48.612
so you're trying to marry her off fast
to the first decent guy you find.

40:48.696 --> 40:50.698
You have no idea.

40:50.781 --> 40:51.615
[scoffs]

40:54.326 --> 40:55.327
[grunts]

40:57.455 --> 40:59.290
- [door slams]
- [exhales deeply]

41:05.045 --> 41:06.380
[Si-woo] Get home safe?

41:10.259 --> 41:12.178
Yeah. H-A-U?

41:13.888 --> 41:15.014
No, no, no.

41:15.097 --> 41:17.308
Keep it professional, text formally.

41:19.059 --> 41:20.644
Forecaster Lee.

41:21.395 --> 41:23.522
Thank you for your hard work today.

41:24.023 --> 41:25.399
Are you still at…

41:27.568 --> 41:29.111
[scoffs]
No way.

41:30.362 --> 41:31.989
Not today.

41:32.072 --> 41:34.074
[quirky music playing]

41:39.705 --> 41:40.581
LEE SI-WOO

41:59.975 --> 42:01.310
[chuckles]

42:07.316 --> 42:09.193
He seriously loves the sky.

42:12.488 --> 42:13.531
[cell phone trills]

42:13.614 --> 42:15.908
[cell phone ringing]

42:15.991 --> 42:17.409
[gasps]

42:17.493 --> 42:18.536
Oh!

42:18.619 --> 42:20.746
- No, no. Hang up!
- [Si-woo] Director Jin?

42:20.829 --> 42:23.040
Oh, Forecaster. How's work?

42:23.123 --> 42:25.584
Good. I'm almost done for the night.

42:25.668 --> 42:27.378
Is there something you wanted?

42:27.461 --> 42:30.839
Oh, I wanted to check in
and make sure everything is all right.

42:30.923 --> 42:34.343
Hey, I bet you thought I'd leave early
and I wouldn't get it done, didn't you?

42:34.426 --> 42:35.970
No, I have faith in you.

42:36.595 --> 42:39.056
Then it must be,
you wanted to see my face?

42:40.474 --> 42:41.559
Definitely not.

42:41.642 --> 42:44.061
Why did you call, then?
It's terribly late.

42:44.144 --> 42:48.399
Uh, well, I… You need to find cases
from other countries

42:48.482 --> 42:50.901
that have fogs like we do,
and I need them in the morning.

42:51.569 --> 42:53.153
- Huh?
- And look into what countries

42:53.237 --> 42:55.406
have local fog advisories,

42:55.489 --> 42:58.325
and what equipment and methods
they use, and their budgets.

42:58.409 --> 42:59.451
Budget's important.

43:00.286 --> 43:01.704
You… You need it tomorrow?

43:02.871 --> 43:04.123
Does this seem like a joke?

43:05.249 --> 43:07.001
Uh, no, ma'am.

43:07.793 --> 43:10.713
Okay. I'm gonna expect this on my desk.

43:10.796 --> 43:12.798
- That's all.
- Okay.

43:14.842 --> 43:15.801
[exhales deeply]

43:16.802 --> 43:18.762
Okay. Great cover.

43:20.222 --> 43:21.473
What?

43:22.391 --> 43:24.184
Why is her wall have to be so high?

43:34.445 --> 43:35.571
Hello.

43:38.532 --> 43:40.909
- Hey.
- Oh, good morning.

43:41.994 --> 43:43.245
[Seok-ho] What's all this?

43:43.329 --> 43:47.041
Oh, Director Jin told me to look up
countries that have fog problems

43:47.124 --> 43:49.209
and the countries
that have local fog advisories.

43:49.293 --> 43:50.669
[gasps]

43:51.337 --> 43:53.422
Wait, were you here all night?

43:53.505 --> 43:55.591
It's nothing new, honestly.

43:55.674 --> 43:57.593
We did it in training.
[chuckles]

43:57.676 --> 44:01.180
Oh, no, your little smile,
it's breaking my heart.

44:01.263 --> 44:04.141
The bags under your eyes
are gonna hang down to your chin.

44:04.224 --> 44:06.810
It's okay. It was important.
Director Jin said it was urgent.

44:07.686 --> 44:09.146
Is it really urgent, though?

44:10.064 --> 44:11.649
It's not just busywork?

44:11.732 --> 44:12.691
What?

44:12.775 --> 44:13.942
[Soo-jin sighs]

44:14.026 --> 44:16.612
- You guys think she did it?
- Yeah.

44:17.696 --> 44:19.948
- Did what?
- There's this…

44:20.032 --> 44:23.994
this thing that the superiors do
to put people in line.

44:24.953 --> 44:27.081
I'm sorry to tell you, it's a prank.

44:28.248 --> 44:29.083
[chuckles]

44:29.750 --> 44:32.086
Hey, she wouldn't. Hey!

44:35.172 --> 44:37.132
- Good morning, everyone.
- Morning.

44:43.389 --> 44:47.351
- What's the deal? Something happened?
- No, ma'am. But I think he has a report.

44:50.020 --> 44:52.481
- Here.
- Hm? What's all this?

44:52.564 --> 44:55.734
It's the report you asked for
when you called last night.

44:56.902 --> 44:59.780
You really needed it today, right?

45:00.531 --> 45:04.785
- I stayed up all night for you.
- I certainly did. Thank you.

45:04.868 --> 45:07.663
Director Jin, you should see this.

45:07.746 --> 45:08.914
What is it?

45:11.458 --> 45:13.460
[tense music playing]

45:15.462 --> 45:16.505
[exhales deeply]

45:19.341 --> 45:20.551
[slams]

45:23.637 --> 45:25.722
- The hell is this, Han?
- Hm?

45:25.806 --> 45:27.933
You're gonna pretend you didn't know that?

45:29.268 --> 45:30.602
WHY DOESN'T KOREA
HAVE FOG ADVISORIES?

45:30.686 --> 45:33.147
INCOMPETENT KMA BLAMES IT
ON TIGHT BUDGET!

45:35.441 --> 45:36.775
REPORTER CHAE YU-JIN

45:38.861 --> 45:40.612
You had no idea this was happening?

45:42.281 --> 45:43.365
[sighs]

45:43.449 --> 45:45.868
[newspaper rustling]

45:48.162 --> 45:50.456
I'm sorry, sir. I wasn't aware.

45:50.539 --> 45:54.626
Seriously? It's by your wife.
You should know. How did this happen?

46:00.174 --> 46:02.176
[tense music playing]

46:27.910 --> 46:30.037
- What is this?
- An article.

46:31.288 --> 46:34.583
The quotes you credited as mine
were not what I told you yesterday.

46:34.666 --> 46:37.211
Reporters should have enough integrity
not to twist facts.

46:37.794 --> 46:39.505
Exactly which part was twisted?

46:39.588 --> 46:40.464
Everything.

46:40.547 --> 46:43.133
I told you why we can't do advisories,
we have no choice.

46:43.217 --> 46:44.718
And that's what the article says.

46:44.801 --> 46:46.136
What's the issue, then?

46:47.971 --> 46:51.099
You must not have understood what I said.
Korea's geography.

46:51.183 --> 46:53.810
The Taebaek and the Hamgyong Mountains
lean toward the east,

46:53.894 --> 46:55.562
and the eastern-facing side
is particularly steep

46:55.646 --> 46:57.105
while the west is totally flat.

46:57.189 --> 47:00.108
The Seoul valley to Wonsan
is long and narrow.

47:00.192 --> 47:02.653
It's the same shape
as the Chugaryeong Tectonic Valley.

47:02.736 --> 47:03.862
Yeah, and?

47:03.946 --> 47:04.821
What about it?

47:05.822 --> 47:06.823
[scoffs]

47:06.907 --> 47:08.742
I'll say it another way for you.

47:08.825 --> 47:11.078
Meteorologists from around the world say

47:11.161 --> 47:13.038
the country with some
of the most fickle weather,

47:13.121 --> 47:15.666
the toughest in the world
to forecast is here,

47:15.749 --> 47:17.125
the Republic of Korea.

47:17.209 --> 47:19.378
It's a peninsula where 70 percent
of the land is mountainous.

47:19.461 --> 47:22.005
We have 11 major rivers
and over 1,000 dams.

47:22.089 --> 47:24.841
Regardless of terrain,
fogs are very localized.

47:24.925 --> 47:26.843
For those reasons,
we can't do local advisories,

47:26.927 --> 47:27.928
it's ineffective.

47:28.011 --> 47:31.390
The only way you'd think we're incompetent
is that you had misunderstood.

47:32.015 --> 47:33.058
[scoffs]

47:33.141 --> 47:34.351
Please.

47:34.851 --> 47:37.396
You explicitly said it requires equipment
we just don't have,

47:37.479 --> 47:39.606
and getting the equipment
is outside our budget.

47:39.690 --> 47:42.734
Which is the excuse that
every government department uses

47:42.818 --> 47:44.319
as cover-up.

47:45.320 --> 47:47.739
- An excuse?
- That's what it is.

47:47.823 --> 47:50.158
Your yearly budget
is over 400 billion won.

47:50.242 --> 47:51.994
If you have that much money,

47:52.077 --> 47:54.621
you can't say that life-saving equipment
is too expensive.

47:54.705 --> 47:57.040
It doesn't make sense
if you know the cost of it.

47:57.124 --> 47:59.251
And lots of other countries
have figured it out.

47:59.334 --> 48:00.377
Say one that does.

48:00.460 --> 48:01.878
The UK, USA,

48:01.962 --> 48:03.380
- Australia, and Japan.
- The UK?

48:04.256 --> 48:06.925
You know the UK's annual budget
for the Meteorological Administration?

48:07.009 --> 48:08.969
1.6 trillion won.

48:09.052 --> 48:10.679
That's four times what we have.

48:10.762 --> 48:12.180
The US? Japan?

48:12.264 --> 48:13.515
- Australia?
- Whatever.

48:13.599 --> 48:15.475
This is why you research
before publishing!

48:15.976 --> 48:18.145
Do your research
and make sure you understand!

48:18.228 --> 48:19.187
And if you can't…

48:21.023 --> 48:23.567
there are people you know
that can check your work.

48:29.656 --> 48:32.409
You didn't intentionally overlook this,
or did you?

48:33.243 --> 48:36.496
Are you acting out of spite?
Letting things slide, so you can hurt me?

48:42.878 --> 48:44.504
[exhales sharply]

48:48.634 --> 48:49.551
It was unintentional.

48:50.844 --> 48:52.679
I'll take care of it from here.

48:52.763 --> 48:54.264
You can go back to your work.

48:58.894 --> 49:00.103
It's your job

49:01.813 --> 49:03.357
to deal with the press.

49:04.107 --> 49:05.317
Deal with it.

49:11.281 --> 49:12.491
You're angry?

49:12.574 --> 49:14.743
Let's find some privacy. We'll talk there.

49:16.370 --> 49:17.621
What are you gonna take care of?

49:18.246 --> 49:19.748
This mess of an article,

49:19.831 --> 49:22.459
I have to take care of it,
'cause that's what I do here.

49:23.543 --> 49:24.628
[sighs]

49:26.088 --> 49:28.048
You have to be ready
if you do stuff like that.

49:28.131 --> 49:30.425
Ha-kyung's smart. There's a reason

49:30.509 --> 49:32.719
she's the youngest director
the division's ever had.

49:32.803 --> 49:34.096
So what now?

49:34.179 --> 49:36.515
You used to confuse probability
of detection with accuracy

49:36.598 --> 49:39.267
when you first started coming here,
but now you're just picking fight.

49:39.351 --> 49:40.811
Why are you bringing that up again?

49:40.894 --> 49:42.270
Come on, you know better than that.

49:42.354 --> 49:43.772
You should've notified me
before submitting.

49:43.855 --> 49:46.441
I tried, I asked you to get me
an interview yesterday.

49:46.525 --> 49:50.070
And I told you to wait! Then I could have
proofread it to double-check!

49:50.654 --> 49:51.488
Double-check?

49:52.072 --> 49:54.408
Reporters don't ask their subjects
to check their work.

49:54.491 --> 49:56.201
It's rude. I'm a journalist.

49:56.284 --> 49:59.204
It's my job to keep an eye on you
and keep you in check.

50:01.873 --> 50:03.083
That's ridiculous.

50:03.166 --> 50:04.960
'Cause you're not logical or factual.

50:05.043 --> 50:06.753
A real journalist
never would have published that.

50:06.837 --> 50:08.672
- That's mean.
- You wouldn't have to lie

50:08.755 --> 50:10.966
- if you were such a great reporter.
- I didn't lie.

50:11.049 --> 50:13.552
- It was the truth, she said everything.
- Lee Si-woo.

50:15.679 --> 50:17.013
You've never met him?

50:26.398 --> 50:27.774
Another fact?

50:36.700 --> 50:37.701
[sighs]

50:40.537 --> 50:41.830
Oh…

50:48.420 --> 50:50.464
Oh, I think she's getting yelled at. Huh?

50:51.131 --> 50:53.759
Probably. She should've known
not to do an interview.

50:54.634 --> 50:57.637
She would've lost
even if she had declined.

50:57.721 --> 51:01.057
'Cause people would think
she's still hung up on him, you know?

51:02.684 --> 51:06.438
Goes to show, breaking up
with a co-worker is even more painful.

51:06.938 --> 51:09.483
Not that marrying one
is anything to brag about.

51:09.566 --> 51:11.735
Just don't date in the workplace.

51:11.818 --> 51:12.819
Hm.

51:22.996 --> 51:24.039
I apologize.

51:24.122 --> 51:26.458
She said she needed help with her article.

51:26.541 --> 51:29.294
I should've chosen my words
much more carefully.

51:29.377 --> 51:30.587
That's true.

51:32.881 --> 51:35.509
What else?
I assume that you called her out.

51:37.093 --> 51:38.929
Yes. I was just so angry.

51:40.055 --> 51:40.972
Well done.

51:43.058 --> 51:46.812
The reporters just want a hit piece
and we're an easy target.

51:46.895 --> 51:47.938
You should get angry.

51:48.688 --> 51:51.733
We take criticism in stride,
but if you think about it,

51:52.317 --> 51:54.736
if these reporters
are not held accountable by us,

51:54.820 --> 51:56.154
who's going to do it?

51:56.238 --> 51:57.614
You did well.

51:58.240 --> 52:00.283
Ah. I have a job for you.

52:01.034 --> 52:02.828
You're gonna write a response article.

52:03.870 --> 52:07.916
Hm? Using logic and facts,
and you'll explain the real reason

52:07.999 --> 52:10.168
we don't do fog advisories in Korea.

52:10.752 --> 52:12.963
I can't let you write that
if it's a direct response.

52:13.839 --> 52:15.048
Get pretty close, though.

52:15.632 --> 52:17.843
- Okay?
- Yes, I'll get started.

52:37.404 --> 52:38.822
How can I help you?

52:43.660 --> 52:47.080
I overheard that they're having you
draft a new article

52:47.831 --> 52:49.165
to clarify your stands on fog.

52:50.375 --> 52:51.585
Yes. And?

52:52.168 --> 52:54.254
I wanted to know your timeline.

52:54.963 --> 52:57.507
It's not set.
I've quite a bit of data to review.

52:58.091 --> 53:01.428
Well, I'd really appreciate your draft
as soon as possible.

53:02.220 --> 53:03.346
I need it

53:04.556 --> 53:06.391
to write the official rebuttal.

53:10.145 --> 53:11.688
You really didn't know?

53:19.821 --> 53:22.407
No, I didn't.

53:25.619 --> 53:27.037
I thought that after marriage,

53:27.120 --> 53:30.206
a couple starts to communicate even more,
be more open.

53:31.207 --> 53:32.834
I've been wrong before.

53:35.462 --> 53:37.547
I can get the draft to you
tomorrow morning.

53:37.631 --> 53:38.548
All right?

53:44.512 --> 53:45.597
[sighs]

53:57.817 --> 53:59.402
What? You what?

54:00.570 --> 54:03.073
She met with a matchmaker,
did the ranking quiz,

54:03.156 --> 54:04.199
and decided to sign you up.

54:05.116 --> 54:06.159
[Mrs. Bae clears throat]

54:06.242 --> 54:07.953
I think it'll be good for you.

54:08.036 --> 54:10.497
Since you've been acting
like such a lovesick baby,

54:11.373 --> 54:14.834
I couldn't sit by any longer.
I know what you're worth.

54:14.918 --> 54:17.712
If you're not going to find
yourself a husband, I will.

54:19.047 --> 54:20.632
Oh, good job. She took it real well.

54:22.467 --> 54:24.844
I did it, 'cause I love you so very much!

54:24.928 --> 54:28.974
Huh? And then you could go and marry
a kind man who is successful.

54:29.057 --> 54:31.434
And everyone at your work
would be impressed, too.

54:31.518 --> 54:33.979
So just forget about Ki-jun already,
that bastard.

54:34.062 --> 54:35.647
I know you know I'm right.

54:36.231 --> 54:37.899
You've got a lot of confidence, Ma.

54:38.525 --> 54:41.236
Can't you be on my side once? Traitor.

54:45.365 --> 54:50.245
[clattering]

54:52.122 --> 54:54.499
[Mrs. Bae] Ha-kyung, what are you doing?

54:54.582 --> 54:57.210
- I think she's gonna leave, Ma.
- What?

54:57.293 --> 54:58.628
You… You're not going, are you?

54:59.671 --> 55:02.716
Go back to the matchmaker
and have her delete the profile.

55:02.799 --> 55:04.300
Shut it down.

55:04.384 --> 55:05.885
You can call me when it's done.

55:06.594 --> 55:09.556
You can't, you know how expensive it was.

55:11.057 --> 55:12.851
- Ha-kyung.
- Wait!

55:12.934 --> 55:15.186
- I knew it! You wouldn't listen!
- I need shoes. Ha-kyung!

55:15.270 --> 55:16.104
[slams]

55:19.774 --> 55:21.609
[car beeping]

55:35.999 --> 55:37.500
[engine starts]

55:43.882 --> 55:45.216
[lock chimes]

55:45.300 --> 55:47.302
[soft music playing]

56:33.139 --> 56:34.140
[sighs]

56:36.017 --> 56:39.938
[keyboard clacking]

56:41.272 --> 56:44.234
UNTITLED5.MP3
SEARCH FILES

56:53.993 --> 56:57.163
[cell phone buzzing]

56:57.247 --> 56:59.415
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

57:03.586 --> 57:06.005
Hello, Director Jin.
Is everything all right?

57:06.089 --> 57:08.466
- [Ha-kyung] Were you asleep?
- No, I wasn't.

57:08.550 --> 57:09.968
Oh, good.

57:10.051 --> 57:15.181
I looked over your report on the UK,
and I'm confused by the translations.

57:15.265 --> 57:16.266
Can you help?

57:26.192 --> 57:27.235
Uh, where is it?

57:27.318 --> 57:29.070
It's on page 12.

57:29.154 --> 57:31.156
In the second chapter.

57:31.239 --> 57:32.866
Okay. One minute.

57:34.075 --> 57:35.201
Okay.

57:36.536 --> 57:37.829
Hm…

57:45.920 --> 57:47.338
INCOMING CALL
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

57:49.841 --> 57:50.758
Yeah?

57:51.426 --> 57:53.720
Page 27, Table 3-1.

57:53.803 --> 57:55.555
Was there a graph, too?

57:57.682 --> 57:59.684
[Si-woo breathes heavily]

57:59.767 --> 58:01.936
[cell phone buzzing]

58:08.902 --> 58:10.153
Yeah?

58:10.236 --> 58:13.323
Is there any reason I can't use
the Sydney case for reference?

58:13.406 --> 58:14.616
It has so many singularities.

58:16.576 --> 58:17.827
Uh…

58:18.703 --> 58:20.121
Are you still there?

58:20.747 --> 58:23.416
Yeah, I'm here. One minute.

58:36.554 --> 58:38.515
[grunting]

58:54.531 --> 58:58.201
[doorbell dings]

59:04.165 --> 59:05.208
What are you doing here?

59:05.291 --> 59:07.669
It's easier than having you call
every five seconds.

59:07.752 --> 59:09.504
Well, I haven't called in 30 minutes, so…

59:09.587 --> 59:11.214
Staying up made me hungry,

59:11.297 --> 59:13.508
so I had to go out, anyway,
to get some food.

59:13.591 --> 59:15.218
And I thought you might want some, too.

59:19.847 --> 59:21.140
Okay.

59:24.644 --> 59:25.728
[Si-woo] Here.

59:29.607 --> 59:31.568
Oh, there are toppings on it.

59:32.485 --> 59:33.403
Yeah, so?

59:33.987 --> 59:36.781
I don't get toppings on pizza.

59:37.991 --> 59:39.993
I can fix that. Here.

59:40.994 --> 59:42.704
Flip one over.

59:43.955 --> 59:45.665
It's not pizza, it's a sandwich.

59:47.542 --> 59:48.960
- Mmm!
- [chuckles]

59:49.669 --> 59:50.670
Is it good?

59:52.547 --> 59:53.548
Have some.

59:55.008 --> 59:56.384
- Flip it?
- Yeah.

59:56.467 --> 59:59.304
- Put them together?
- Just like the sandwich. Yeah.

59:59.387 --> 01:00:01.306
- [chuckles]
- You'll like it.

01:00:01.389 --> 01:00:02.557
- Cheers.
- Yeah.

01:00:04.434 --> 01:00:05.518
It's good, right?

01:00:06.394 --> 01:00:09.606
- Dig in, please.
- [giggling]

01:00:10.398 --> 01:00:12.400
[calm music playing]

01:00:22.994 --> 01:00:25.455
Yeah, this one was from the UK.

01:00:25.538 --> 01:00:28.333
There should be
the original copy of the article.

01:00:28.416 --> 01:00:29.834
- Can you find it?
- Oh, yeah.

01:00:30.668 --> 01:00:31.878
[Si-woo yawns]
Here it is.

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:34.380
I marked all of the most important parts
in blue for you.

01:00:34.464 --> 01:00:35.632
See there?

01:00:37.300 --> 01:00:39.344
I think it needs to be simpler.

01:00:39.427 --> 01:00:42.180
- Hm?
- You should break it down.

01:00:42.263 --> 01:00:43.806
[Si-woo] What do you think?

01:00:47.101 --> 01:00:48.811
I think it's good for a draft.

01:00:49.395 --> 01:00:50.521
You think?

01:01:03.076 --> 01:01:05.078
["Mind Warning" by ONEW playing]

01:01:05.161 --> 01:01:06.496
[chuckles]

01:01:09.457 --> 01:01:11.834
[Si-woo] How do you feel, though,
about me?

01:01:14.045 --> 01:01:15.588
I shouldn't have revealed it.

01:01:16.339 --> 01:01:17.548
Sorry.

01:01:22.095 --> 01:01:23.429
I'm not sorry at all.

01:01:25.223 --> 01:01:28.851
Why would I be sorry that you
could see I wanna be with you?

01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:33.898
I really do.

01:01:33.981 --> 01:01:36.401
["Mind Warning" by ONEW continues]

01:01:57.755 --> 01:01:59.757
["Mind Warning" by ONEW continues]

01:02:26.492 --> 01:02:27.827
[sighs]

01:02:33.750 --> 01:02:34.876
[exhales heavily]

01:02:40.089 --> 01:02:42.842
[toilet flushes]

01:02:46.888 --> 01:02:48.014
[sighs]

01:03:00.109 --> 01:03:02.069
Oh? Why are you here so late?

01:03:02.153 --> 01:03:04.489
Oh, it's been so busy.

01:03:05.072 --> 01:03:07.992
I missed my shot. Si-woo has a girlfriend.

01:03:10.536 --> 01:03:11.704
Where did you hear that?

01:03:12.872 --> 01:03:15.041
Everybody's been talking about her.

01:03:15.625 --> 01:03:17.960
He said that she works here at KMA.

01:03:20.838 --> 01:03:24.675
♪ So now this time ♪

01:03:24.759 --> 01:03:28.638
♪ I'll make you mine ♪

01:03:28.721 --> 01:03:30.223
♪ This time… ♪

01:03:30.306 --> 01:03:31.933
[Ha-kyung] Isn't it beautiful?

01:03:33.434 --> 01:03:34.685
[Si-woo] It is.

01:03:35.686 --> 01:03:37.772
Sunrise is my favorite part of the day.

01:03:38.397 --> 01:03:40.316
I didn't know you're a morning person.

01:03:40.399 --> 01:03:41.567
[chuckles]

01:03:42.777 --> 01:03:43.986
Tell me more.

01:03:50.284 --> 01:03:53.412
I don't wanna sell this place yet.

01:03:56.874 --> 01:03:58.376
It makes me think of what happened.

01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:01.629
I need some new memories here,
so the old ones will fade.

01:04:05.800 --> 01:04:07.051
Tell me more.

01:04:07.635 --> 01:04:10.054
[chuckles]
Well, what do you wanna know about me?

01:04:10.680 --> 01:04:11.848
Everything.

01:04:12.598 --> 01:04:16.561
I wanna know everything. If that's okay.

01:04:17.228 --> 01:04:18.479
Everything.

01:04:21.941 --> 01:04:23.359
Didn't I ask for discretion?

01:04:24.110 --> 01:04:25.945
Well, we're not at the office, so…

01:04:26.028 --> 01:04:27.238
[chuckles]

01:04:28.114 --> 01:04:32.285
You know we have to end this
if they ever found out, you know?

01:04:33.995 --> 01:04:35.121
I know.

01:04:36.581 --> 01:04:40.543
And I'd have to put up walls to keep them
from getting suspicious of us.

01:04:42.086 --> 01:04:43.254
I know.

01:04:44.171 --> 01:04:45.464
I can take it.

01:04:48.718 --> 01:04:51.387
[Si-woo]
Visibility is the maximum distance

01:04:51.470 --> 01:04:52.889
that can be seen with the naked eye.

01:04:52.972 --> 01:04:54.849
[Seok-ho] You have a girlfriend?

01:05:02.565 --> 01:05:04.275
No. Not right now.

01:05:05.026 --> 01:05:07.570
- You'll have it soon?
- Yeah, of course. Right away.

01:05:07.653 --> 01:05:09.989
What? She's messing with him, right?

01:05:10.072 --> 01:05:12.491
[Soo-jin] She must be.
Maybe he did something.

01:05:22.543 --> 01:05:24.462
[Si-woo]
Depending on the surrounding conditions,

01:05:24.545 --> 01:05:28.007
the naked eyesight
may be heavily distorted.

01:05:29.383 --> 01:05:33.763
I'd appreciate if you'd avoid small talk
during working hours, Forecaster Lee.

01:05:34.430 --> 01:05:36.015
Thanks for this. You may go.

01:05:36.933 --> 01:05:38.559
[Si-woo] It can be narrowed.

01:05:39.685 --> 01:05:41.646
Yes, can I help you?

01:05:41.729 --> 01:05:43.689
Uh, no. I'm all good.

01:05:43.773 --> 01:05:45.775
[romantic music playing]

01:05:46.859 --> 01:05:48.819
[Si-woo] And it can be distorted.

01:05:50.363 --> 01:05:53.157
[Ha-kyung] I don't ever want people
to know that I'm dating a colleague.

01:05:53.240 --> 01:05:54.492
[Si-woo] I know that.

01:05:55.493 --> 01:05:57.119
What if we break down each area?

01:05:57.203 --> 01:06:00.915
And we can emphasize the valleys,
streams, and any other unique areas.

01:06:11.217 --> 01:06:13.094
[Si-woo] It seems like right now,

01:06:13.177 --> 01:06:16.639
our visibility is low,
so we'll have to be careful.

01:06:18.307 --> 01:06:21.519
What happens if someone catches us?

01:06:22.561 --> 01:06:25.147
We'd fuss up and end things.

01:06:26.524 --> 01:06:27.525
Oh.

01:06:28.192 --> 01:06:29.318
That's exciting.

01:06:30.611 --> 01:06:33.489
I can't go through all that.
I've learned my lesson.

01:06:34.115 --> 01:06:35.324
Okay?

01:06:36.993 --> 01:06:38.995
[romantic music playing]

01:07:04.061 --> 01:07:07.857
[Si-woo] We all ran into bad weather,
dense fog,

01:07:07.940 --> 01:07:11.235
yellow dust, unexpected rain, or snow.

01:07:11.318 --> 01:07:13.821
[line ringing]

01:07:21.620 --> 01:07:23.622
[sobbing]

01:07:30.838 --> 01:07:31.839
[sighs]

01:07:45.227 --> 01:07:46.645
[line rings]

01:07:46.729 --> 01:07:49.482
[Si-woo] But bad weather
teaches us something.

01:07:49.565 --> 01:07:50.608
[sniffles]

01:07:52.777 --> 01:07:54.862
[cell phone buzzes]

01:07:54.945 --> 01:07:58.365
[Si-woo] It teaches us
that the best way to improve visibility

01:07:58.449 --> 01:08:03.954
is to be brave and move closer
to reduce your distance from the target.

01:08:25.559 --> 01:08:26.477
I'm late.
[gasps]

01:08:27.228 --> 01:08:28.229
[Si-woo groans]

01:08:39.198 --> 01:08:41.200
[groaning]

01:08:46.413 --> 01:08:47.706
I'm not ready yet.

01:08:47.790 --> 01:08:50.209
- Oh, no, we can't go in together.
- We're gonna be late, though.

01:08:50.292 --> 01:08:51.794
Not we, just you.

01:08:52.586 --> 01:08:54.171
[rapid footsteps]

01:08:55.464 --> 01:08:56.423
[chuckles]

01:08:59.218 --> 01:09:00.427
EFFECTIVENESS OF FOG ADVISORIES
AND CASES FROM ABROAD

01:09:06.267 --> 01:09:12.773
[cell phone buzzing]

01:09:17.194 --> 01:09:19.196
[tense music playing]

01:09:23.826 --> 01:09:24.994
Hello?

01:09:27.955 --> 01:09:29.957
["Mind Warning" by ONEW playing]

01:09:53.355 --> 01:09:55.983
[Seok-ho] How did you cross paths
with Director Jin this morning?

01:09:56.066 --> 01:09:57.484
- We met on our way here.
- Pardon?

01:09:57.568 --> 01:09:58.402
It was a coincidence.

01:09:58.485 --> 01:10:01.363
[Ki-jun] Who said you could
keep crossing lines like that?

01:10:01.447 --> 01:10:03.866
Did you want to see
how I would react if I saw you with him?

01:10:03.949 --> 01:10:06.035
[Ha-kyung] Call me outside like this
one more time…

01:10:06.118 --> 01:10:07.203
Forecaster Lee, you…
[gasps]

01:10:07.286 --> 01:10:09.163
[Si-woo] Do you know of a heart
that asks for permission to beat?

01:10:09.246 --> 01:10:11.957
[gasps]
Get it together, Forecaster Lee!

01:10:12.041 --> 01:10:13.709
[Soo-jin] It's the Metropolitan Office.

01:10:13.792 --> 01:10:15.920
They're saying the rain echo
over Seoul looks abnormal.

01:10:16.003 --> 01:10:17.296
Could you take a look?

01:10:17.379 --> 01:10:18.297
[electricity crackles]

01:10:18.380 --> 01:10:19.381
[beeping]

01:10:19.465 --> 01:10:20.966
[thunder rumbles]
